  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/nh-rsa-data/blob/96bd0a247d4463e2ae692310c0fdd17ec563a46c/rsa_html/LV/541-A/541-A-9.htm",
  "statuteText": "541-A:9 Rulemaking Register. –\n\n[Paragraph I effective until January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I set out below.]\nI. The director of legislative services shall publish directly online a weekly rulemaking register which shall contain:\n(a) Notice of intended rulemaking actions.\n(b) Notice of rules adopted under RSA 541-A:14, RSA 541-A:18, and RSA 541-A:19.\n(c) Nonconfidential opinions of the attorney general under RSA 541-A:28.\n(d) Final objections under RSA 541-A:13, V.\n(e) Notices of continued or postponed public comment hearings under RSA 541-A:11.\n(f) Notices of declaratory rulings issued pursuant to rules adopted under RSA 541-A:16, I(d).\n(g) Notice for the submission of comments on possible rulemaking under RSA 541-A:11, VIII.\n(h) Publication of notice of the list of regulated toxic air pollutants and classifications by the department of environmental services under RSA 125-I:4.\n(i) At the request of any agency, any other notices or documents related to rulemaking, at the discretion of the director.\n(j) A list of proposals filed under RSA 541-A:12, I and proposed interim rules filed under RSA 541-A:19, II, and placed on the agenda for committee review at a regularly scheduled or special committee meeting.\n[Paragraph I effective January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I set out above.]\nI. The director of the division of administrative rules for the office of legislative services shall publish directly online a weekly rulemaking register which shall contain:\n(a) Notices of intended rulemaking actions;\n(b) Notices, once a month, of adopted rules;\n(c) Nonconfidential opinions of the attorney general under RSA 541-A:28;\n(d) Final objections under RSA 541-A:13, V;\n(e) Notices of continued or postponed public comment hearings under RSA 541-A:11;\n(f) Notices of declaratory rulings issued pursuant to rules adopted under RSA 541-A:16, I(d);\n(g) Notices for the submission of comments on possible rulemaking under RSA 541-A:11, VIII;\n(h) Notice of the list of regulated toxic air pollutants and classifications by the department of environmental services under RSA 125-I:4;\n(i) At the request of any agency, any other notices or documents related to rulemaking, at the discretion of the director; and\n(j) A list of proposals filed under RSA 541-A:12, I and proposed interim rules filed under RSA 541-A:19, II, and placed on the agenda for committee review at a regularly scheduled or special committee meeting.\n[Paragraph I-a effective until January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I-a set out below.]\nI-a. Prior to publication, the director of legislative services may correct clarity, formatting, typographical, spelling, and punctuation errors, as well as unintentional errors in references and citations in a submission. Consistent with RSA 541-A:6, II, the director shall notify the agency prior to publication of the notice of any amendments made to the notice and may set a deadline for agency comment on the amendments.\n[Paragraph I-a effective January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I-a set out above.]\nI-a. Prior to publication, the director may correct clarity, formatting, typographical, spelling, and punctuation errors, as well as unintentional errors in references and citations in a submission. Consistent with RSA 541-A:6, II, the director shall notify the agency prior to publication of the notice of any amendments made to the notice and may set a deadline for agency comment on the amendments.\n[Paragraph I-b effective until January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I-b set out below.]\nI-b. The date of publication of the rulemaking register shall be the date on which the register is available to the public on the general court information services web site.\n[Paragraph I-b effective January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I-b set out above.]\nI-b. The date of publication of the rulemaking register shall be the date on which the register is available to the public on the general court information services website.\n[Paragraph I-c effective until January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I-c set out below.]\nI-c. The director of legislative services may prescribe the specific electronic file format for all documents provided by state agencies for inclusion in the register.\n[Paragraph I-c effective January 1, 2027; see also paragraph I-c set out above.]\nI-c. The director may prescribe the specific electronic file format for all documents provided by state agencies for inclusion in the register.\nII. The rulemaking register shall be made available free of charge.\nIII. The rulemaking register shall be sent by email to all members of the general court."
